  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses exclusively on the maximum outcome, preferring the lottery with the higher maximum. The individual in the verbal report acknowledges the importance of the maximum possible amount, stating they would have needed a 'considerably higher' amount in B to choose it — implying that the 4000 Euro maximum of A played a role in their decision. While they mention the certainty of B as 'decisive,' their counterfactual reasoning ('I would have chosen B only if...') reveals that the maximum outcome was a critical threshold in their evaluation. Thus, although certainty is mentioned as a factor, the justification hinges on the insufficiency of B’s maximum outcome. This aligns with the logic of the decision reason, which prioritizes the more favorable maximum outcome. The individual’s reasoning is consistent with using the maximum outcome as a decisive criterion, even if framed in contrast to certainty.",
